tration Nursing Physical Plant President Provost and Academic Affairs Registrar Religion Sport Exercise and Wellness Student Support Services Theatre Search directory Grid List Admissions Tatum Dean Campus Visit Coordinator Admissions Health Information and Quality Assurance Specialist at Seneca Family of Agencies (2022-2024) | Youth Counselor at Seneca Family of Agencies (2021-2022) | English Teacher at Chungdahm Learning Inc. in South Korea (2019-2020) LaNae Fuerst Admissions Counselor Admissions I taught Family and Consumer Sciences (FACS) for three years in Gettysburg, S.D. I then took a job closer to home and taught FACS for three years at Corsica-Stickney, before becoming an admissions counselor at Dakota Wesleyan University. Rachel Giblin Associate Director of Admissions Admissions Janet Greenway Graduate & Online Enrollment Coordinator Admissions 1 yr. (1989): Dakota Wesleyan University: Resident Director of Dayton Hall, 4 yrs. (1990-1994): Dakota Wesleyan University: Admissions Counselor, 29 yrs. (1994-2023): Mitchell Technical College: Admissions Counselor, Career Services, Academic Advising, and Registrar Corbin Kramer Performing Arts Talent Coordinator Admissions, Music, Theatre Laurie Martin Enrollment Services Specialist Admissions Queen of Peace Hospital (Radiologic Technologist, 15 years), City of Mitchell (Communications Specialist, 10+ years), Martin Group (Administrative Assistant, 9 years) Katie Roth Head Esports Coach Admissions I have worked as a childcare teacher for six years and as a Registered Behavior Technician for two and a half years. Megan Sarne Admissions Counselor Admissions Taught for three years at Red Rock Central in Lamberton, Minnesota, and two years at Longfellow Elementary in Mitchell, South Dakota. Fredel Thomas, MBA Vice President of Admissions, Marketing and Technology Admissions, Marketing and Communications, Information Technology Fredel started her career at DWU as director of the Kelly Center for Entrepreneurship, where she taught entrepreneurial leadership courses and served as a resource for regional businesses in South Dakota. She was named dean of admissions in 2015 and was promoted to vice president of admissions and marketing in 2018. As an extension to her work at DWU, Fredel served as chair of the Council on College Admissions in South Dakota, is a board member of the Dakota  Association for College Admission Counseling, serves on the South Dakota Freedom Scholarship Advisory Council, is an affiliate for Credo, a higher education consulting firm, and a frequent speaker for the National Small College Enrollment Conference. Prior to DWU, Fredel worked 12 years in the telecommunications and technology industry as a programmer, quality assurance officer, project manager and director of product management. She has served as a board member for the Weekend Snack Pack, the Abbott House, the Mitchell Area Chamber of Commerce, the Safe Place of Eastern South Dakota, and Avera Queen of Peace. She is active in her church where she leads youth group. Advancement Kitty Allen, M.S.A. Vice President of Institutional Advancement Advancement Kitty is responsible for oversight and implementation of strategic initiatives for university fundraising and alumni relations. She is also a key contact for DWU’s United Methodist constituency. Before coming to Mitchell, Allen served as the director of the Appalachian Local Pastors School a United Methodist Course of Study School located in Barbourville, Ken., for nine years, and she worked in advancement at Asbury Theological Seminary in Wilmore, Ken., for several years prior. Vickie Gukeisen Administrative Assistant for Institutional Advancement Advancement Jory Hansen, M.A. Director of Development Advancement Kelsey Morgan Alumni Engagement Associate Advancement Program Assistant at the Dakotas and Minnesota Methodist Foundations (2016-2025) Athletic Training Rebecca Buchholz, DAT Director of Clinical Education | Assistant Professor of Athletic Training Athletic Training Began working at CNOS as an athletic trainer in June of 2023 at South Sioux City High School. Randi Christensen, M.A. Director of Athletic Training Services Athletic Training She is a certified athletic trainer and adviser for the DWU Athletic Training Club. She has taught in the CAATE accredited athletic training program and also teaches and advises in the sport, exercise and wellness curriculum. She provides the AT coverage for DWU’s volleyball team and the women’s basketball team while mentoring the graduate assistant’s programs. Caitlin Place, ATC Associate Athletic Trainer Athletic Training Athletic Trainer - St. Cloud Orthopedics (2016-2020) | Athletic Trainer - Sanford Health (2020-2025) | NREMT (2021-present) Trent Suckut, MAT, ATC Associate Athletic Trainer Athletic Training Mackenzie Vandenburg, MAT, ATC Associate Athletic Trainer Athletic Training Associate Athletic Trainer at Culver-Stockton College (August 2024-May 2026) Dan Wagner, Ed.D. Program Director of Athletic Training | Athletic Training Preceptor | Professor in the Athletic Training Program Athletic Training As preceptor, Wagner works with the wrestling team and rehabilitates DWU’s injured athletes. He also holds certification from the National Athletic Trainers Association; is a member of the South Dakota Athletic Trainers’ Association; and is an American Safety and Health Institute CPR Pro. Matthew Zens, DPT Professor of Athletic Training Athletic Training Athletics Robert Atwater Assistant Track and Field and Cross Country Coach Athletics Celeste Beck Associate Head Coach of Women’s Basketball | Senior Women’s Administrator Athletics Bailey Berg Assistant Football Coach | Defensive Backs Athletics (2022-2023) Northern State University: Defensive Graduate Assistant / Defensive Backs, (2020-2022) Minnesota State University, Mankato: Cornerbacks / Director of Football Operations, (2018-2020) Minnesota State University, Mankato: Defensive Line Assistant / Director of Footb