on to the State Bar of South Dakota (September 2015) Ben Johnson, M.Ed. Assistant Baseball Coach Athletics Winona State University (Baseball Coach - 2 years as Grad Assistant and 2 years as Assistant) Alex Kretzschmar, M.S. Head Football Coach | Offensive Coordinator Athletics North Park University (Wide Receivers Coach), St. Ambrose University (Wide Receivers Coach, Video Coordinator), Colby College (Quarterbacks Coach, Wide Receivers Coach, Video Coordinator, Academic Coordinator), Dakota State University (Offensive Coordinator, Recruiting Coordinator), Valley City State University (Quarterbacks Coach, Wide Receivers Coach, Video Coordinator) John Lynch, DPT Head Women's Wrestling Coach Athletics Jeff Meyerink Head Golf Coach Athletics Martin Mueller Head Men's Wrestling Coach Athletics Graduate Assistant at South Dakota State 2021 Sam Nicholson Head Men's Basketball Coach Athletics Assistant Coach - Dakota Wesleyan University (2023-2025) | Assistant Coach - Dakota State University (2022-2023) | Graduate Assistant - Concordia St. Paul (2020-2022) | Student Assistant - University of South Dakota (2015-2020) Sina Nu'u Assistant Volleyball Coach Athletics I attended Texas Lutheran University to study Kinesiology and play Division III volleyball in the SCAC. While in college, I spent time in the club volleyball world working with young indoor and sand volleyball athletes. After completing my undergrad, I attended Hastings College to earn a Master's degree in Teaching and serve as the Graduate Assistant for the Bronco volleyball team. Caitlin Ostbye, MSAL, CSCS Associate Registrar | Assistant Strength and Conditioning Coach | Assistant Track and Field Coach Registrar, Athletics Graduate Assistant for Track and Field and Strength and Conditioning at Augustana University (2025), Student Strength and Conditioning Assistant - Northwestern College (2020-2024), Strength and Conditioning Intern at University of North Carolina Chapel Hill (2023) Nicolas Reinhard, MBA Head Men's Soccer Coach Athletics Head Men's Soccer Coach at Dakota Wesleyan University (NAIA), Assistant Coach at Trevecca University (NCAA D2), Assistant Men's and Women's Soccer Coach at Donelson Christian Academy (High School) Jordan Riewer Assistant Men's Basketball Coach Athletics (2015–2016) Professional Basketball Player: Oettinger Rockets (German ProA),  (2016–2017) Professional Basketball Player: BK NH Ostrava (Czech Republic NBL), (2017–2018) Assistant Men’s Basketball Coach: Minnesota State University Moorhead, (2018–2019) Professional Basketball Player: Central District Lions (South Australia Premier League), (2019-2020) Professional Basketball Player: KK Skrljevo in Croatia, (2020–2021) Professional Basketball Player: Newcastle Falcons (Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia), (2022–2023) Player Development Coach: Academy of Holy Angels (Richfield, M.N.), (2023–2024) Sales Representative: Airborne Athletics (Dr. Dish Shooting Machines), Minneapolis, M.N., (2024–2025) Assistant Men’s Basketball Coach: University of Minnesota Duluth Matthew Schwaerzler Sports Information Director Athletics Saint Martin's University (Assistant Athletic Director of Communications, April 2024 - May 2025), Portland Pickles Baseball Team (Director of Digital Marketing & Public Relations, Jan. 2023 - April 2024) Jared Seckel Head Track and Field and Cross Country Coach Athletics Cassey Ver Hey Head Cheer and Dance Coach Athletics Marlene Warnke Business Manager for Athletics Athletics Dakota Wesleyan University, Faculty Secretary, 1990-99 | Dakota Wesleyan University, Campus Life Administrative Assistant, 1999-2005 | Dakota Wesleyan University, Athletics Business Manager 2005-present | Warnke has also served on various committees both on and off-campus. Lindsay Wilber Head Volleyball Coach Athletics Behavioral Sciences Julie Hart Schutte, M.S. Assistant Professor of Psychology Behavioral Sciences DWU (Psychology Adjunct, 2019-2024), Mitchell Technical College (Instructor of Human Services and Sociology, 2015-2024), Mitchell Technical College (Counselor and Disability Coordinator, 2003-2015), LifeQuest (Director of Career Connections, 1996-2003), Mitchell Technical Institute (Testing and Placement Specialist, 1993-1996), DWU (Assistant Director of Admissions, 1992-1993), DWU (Admissions Counselor, 1989-1992) Alex Richardson, M.S. Assistant Professor of Psychology Behavioral Sciences Biology Julie Olson, Ed.D. Assistant Professor of Biology Biology Southeast Technical College (Natural Sciences lead instructor (Anatomy, Physiology, Physics, and Environmental Science) 2021-2024), Mitchell Senior High (High School science teacher (Dual credit Biology, Environmental Science, Chemistry, and Alternative School Science) 1992-2021), Dakota Wesleyan University (Adjunct Professor (Microbiology, Secondary Science Teaching Methods, Biology) 1988-2020), Emery High School (High school science and math teacher (Biology, Physics, Chemistry, Geometry, Algebra I and II, Senior Math) 1988-1992) Brian Patrick, Ph.D. Professor of Biology Biology Kat Sestrick, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Biology Biology Bookstore Lori Solberg DWU Store Manager Bookstore I was an assistant merchandiser with JC Penney’s before coming to Dakota Wesleyan University. Business Tracy Dice, DBA Associate Professor of Business and Economics Business Jessica Dollahon, DBA Assistant Director of the Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship | Director of the MBA Program | Assistant Professor of Management Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship, Business Essendant (Business Development Specialist & Consultant), Lagasse-Sweet (Vendor Coordinator), Multiple Co's (Insurance Agent) Diana Goldammer, Ed.D. Associate Professor | Director of the Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Business, Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Dr. Goldammer started her professional career as a high school English teacher. She moved into the private sector and worked in telecommunications and agribusiness. Here at DWU, Dr. Goldammer worked in public relations, went into student life in 2009, and in 2019 joined the business faculty. Steven Horan, DBA, CPA, CGMA Assistant Professor of Accounting and Finance Business CFO | Senior Accountant | Financial Accountant and Public Accounting Stuart Keenan, M.A., M.S. Assistant Professor of Business Business Cleary University (Registrar), Ball State University (Assistant Director for Transcripts), Muncie Indiana Transit System (Lead Dispatcher), Indiana University East (Adjunct Professor in History) Christine Mauszycki, M.P.A., CPA Professor of Accounting | Keith B. Miller Endowed Chair of the Musick Family Department of Business Business Business owner Leah Mellegaard Administrative Assistant Business Dave Mitchell Professor Emeritus, Business and Economics Business Prior to Dakota Wesleyan, Mitchell was a systems analyst for Procter and Gamble and taught at Boston University. He has received both the Sears Award and Clarke Award for Teaching Excellence. His scholarly activities have focused on policy analysis and public presentations relating local and national public issues. Beyond DWU, Mitchell has been an active leader in the United Methodist Church and in local political and community activities. The Rev. Matt Morrison, M.Div. Director of Practical Church Leadership Business Pastor, Worship Leader, Business Owner, Business Management Tera Starr, M.S. Assistant Professor of Marketing Business Worked at Mattress Firm for 18 years (District Manager, Regional VP & VP of Learning & Development) | Business owner for 4 years Business Office Kerri Fahey Accounts Receivable Specialist Business Office Abra Auto Body & Glass, Palace Builders, Guidehouse Julie Granger Payroll Specialist Business Office Megan Heidinger Business Accountant Business Office Rural Office of Community Services (CFO) | GreatLife Golf and Fitness (Manager/Bookkeeper) Eli Kortan Accounts Payable Specialist Business Office Jasmine Krempges Business Services Coordinator Business Office Jodi Landgaard, MBA Vice President of Finance & Administration Business Office Worked 20 years in corporate and private industries. Landgaard worked for 16 years at a public community college in Minnesota. She began her role as VP of Finance & Administration in August 2023. Campus Life Amun Collins Resident Director Campus Life Admissions Host Abby Ferris Residence Life Lead Campus Life Donna Gerlach, RN Campus Nurse Campus Life Professional Excellence Award for Staff (2003-2004), Supervisor of the Semester for work Study (2009), Recognize for 20 years of service (2019), CPR certified, Certified in Mental Health First Aid Jesus Herrera Resident Director Campus Life Personal Trainer at True Fitness Kimberly Lienemann, M.A., LPC-MH, QMHP Campus Counselor Campus Life I started working in the Behavioral Health field 30 years ago, and I became a licensed therapist in 2004 in Nebraska. The majority of my career was spent in residential, long term, treatment centers for adolescents and adults including four years on an acute psychiatric unit of a hospital in Omaha. I held a variety of clinical supervisory and staff training positions during my years in residential. I started working in private practice in 2016. Licensed Professional Counselor - Mental Health (LPC-MH) South Dakota 2018 - Current. Heather Miller-Cink Dean of Students Campus Life Heather brings 35 years of experience in education, including 14 years as a choral music educator and 21 years in high school administration. She spent nearly three decades of her career in Osseo Area Schools, a diverse district just north of Minneapolis. Her work has centered on collaborative leadership, fostering a positive school culture, and promoting equitable student achievement. The Rev. Anthony Purcell, Ph.D. Campus Pastor Campus Life Senior Pastor at Lake Gibson United Methodist Church, Visiting Assistant Professor of Religion at Florida Southern College, Teaching Associate and Adjunct Professor at Emory University, Youth Minister at Lithia Springs United Methodist Church Taryn Ragels, M. Div. Associate Campus Pastor Campus Life Lead Pastor At Fusion Church (Mitchell, SD) (2020-Present), Director of Ministries at Fusion Church (2017-2020), Community Life and College Ministry Assistant at GracePoint Wesleyan Church (Brookings, SD) Chemistry Bethany Melroe Lehrman, Ph.D. Professor of Chemistry Chemistry Dr. Bethany Melroe Lehrman is a professor of chemistry; dean of the Donna Starr Christen College of Healthcare, Fitness and Sciences; and CHAOS club’s faculty adviser at DWU. In fall 2015, she received a HOPES grant, which allowed DWU students the opportunity to work with and teach science to fifth-graders from L.B. Williams Elementary in Mitchell. She is also a member of many professional affiliations: American Chemical Society (ACS), ACS Division of Chemical Education, Phi Lambda Upsilon (National Honorary Chemical Society), Phi Kappa Phi (Multidisciplinary Honor Society) and Gamma Sigma Delta (Honor Society of Agriculture). Awards: DWU Clarke Award for Teaching Excellence in 2021, DWU Exemplary Teacher Award in 2017, and DWU Faculty Professional Excellence Award in 2015 Paula Mazzer, Ph.D. Professor of Biochemistry Chemistry Her postdoctoral research was with the Environmental Molecular Science Institute at Ohio State University. She taught at Old Dominion University, Norfolk, Va., before coming to DWU. She is a member of the South Dakota EPSCoR BioSNTR team, a statewide NSF-funded project for undergraduate research, and is a recipient of the Faculty Fellowship Grant through South Dakota BRIN (a statewide NIH-funded project). Communications Krista Belanger, Ph.D. Associate Professor of Communications Communications Criminal Justice Joel Reinesch, M.A. Associate Professor of Criminal Justice | Faculty Athletic Representative Criminal Justice Joel is a Marine Corps (Infantry) veteran of two combat deployments in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom. Not long after being Honorably Discharged in 2006, he started with the Mitchell Police Department. There, he held the ranks of Patrol Officer, Detective/Investigator and also Patrol Sergeant. Joel completed his undergrad officially in 2013 and his Master's in 2018. He worked for the Mitchell PD for more than 11 years before being hired by Dakota Wesleyan, his alma mater. Digital Media and Design Kyle Herges, MFA Professor of Digital Media and Design | Dean of the College of Arts and Humanities Digital Media and Design User Experience Designer (Current), Software Designer, Web Designer, Graphic Designer, Entrepreneur Education Mindy Childs, M.Ed. Associate Professor of Education Education Mindy has 22 years of experience teaching K-12 special education. From 2006-2022, she instructed students, in a resource room setting, for the Mitchell School District at both Longfellow Elementary School and Mitchell High School. Additionally, during her time at Longfellow, she codirected Longfellow's LEAP program, a programmed designed to address academic gaps and facilitate direct instruction to students in the areas of reading and mathematics. From 2000-2006, Mindy taught special education for the Watertown School District and was one of the founding teachers for the school district’s behavior program known as Project SUCCESS. Ashley Digmann, Ed.D. Dean of the Ron and Sheilah Gates College of Business, Education and Social Science | Education Department Chair Education 7th-grade math/science teacher at Hopson Middle School in Barrow, AK. High School math teacher at Aberdeen Central HS in Aberdeen, S.D.  She was awarded the Exemplary Teaching Award from DWU in 2015 and the Clarke Award for Teaching Excellence in 2016. She is a member of the South Dakota Council of Teachers of Mathematics, the National Council of Teachers in Mathematics, Sigma Zeta honor society, and is a local Phi Kappa Phi honor society member. She is also the chair of the IRB committee. Craig Mock, M.A. Assistant Professor of Education Education Adjunct Instructor (Dakota Wesleyan University) | Instructor/Career Advisor (Mount Marty University) | Senior High Administrator (Mitchell Senior High School) | Junior/Senior High Administrator (Howard School District) | Instructor (Mount Marty College) | Secondary Social Studies Teacher (Stillman Valley Senior High School) | Secondary Social Studies Teacher (Grant-Deuel Senior High School) Katie Schroeder, M.Ed. Assistant Professor of Education Education L.B. Williams Elementary Teacher (Mitchell School District,  2011-2026), Renberg Elementary Teacher (Sioux Falls School District, 2010-2011) April Teel Education Support Specialist Education Melissa Weber, Ed.D. Associate Dean of Strategic Initiatives | Associate Professor of Education | Master of Arts in Education Director Education, Provost and Academic Affairs Canistota School District (ELA Teacher, Librarian, Assistant Principal, Curriculum Director) from 2007-2018; Bridgewater School District (ELA Teacher) from 2005-2007 Tressa Wede, Ed.D. Director of Education and Community Engagement | Associate Professor of Education Education 5th Grade Teacher (LBW Elementary, Mitchell, SD), Gifted and Talented Teacher and Differentiation Specialist (Watertown, SD), 6th Grade Teacher (Irene Elementary School, Irene, SD) Awards: LBW Teacher of the Year in 2007, SDEA South Dakota Teacher to Remember in 2009, ING Unsung Hero Award in 2012, Mitchell Convention and Visitors Bureau Tourism Excellence Award in 2016, Carl Sprunger Outstanding Educator Award in 2017, Honored Women Educators of South Dakota in 2018. English and Languages Barbara Duffey, Ph.D. Professor of English English and Languages She is a published poet, with a chapbook, “The Circus of Forgetting,” and two more books of poetry, “Simple Machines” and “I Might Be Mistaken.” She was also the recipient of a $25,000 Creative Writing Fellowship from the National Endowment for the Arts in 2014, and “Simple Machines” won the Washington Prize from the D.C.-based literary nonprofit The Word Works in summer 2015. The award includes publication and a $1,500 cash prize. She also was nominated for a Pushcart Prize for two poems in 2015, and was the South Dakota State Poetry Society winner in 2013 for chapbook contest with “Four Quarters to a Section.” Taya Sazama, M.A. Assistant Professor of English English and Languages I am co-editor for a forthcoming collection entitled Virginia Woolf: Profession and Performance through Clemson UP (2025) and have written reviews for Jane Austen, Early and Late by Freya Johnston and Victorian Bestseller: The Life of Dinah Craik by Karen Bourrier. In 2015, I published an article \"Theory in Practice in the High School Classroom: Using The Kite Runner to Teach Literary Theory\" with the Minnesota English Journal Online. I have presented my research at numerous conferences, but I have been especially involved with the Jane Austen Society of North America (JASNA) and the British Women Writers Association (BWWA). Timothy Ziegenhagen, Ph.D. Associate Professor of English English and Languages Grand Valley State University, visiting assistant professor (1999-2000) | Northland College, professor (2000-2024) Financial Aid Kristy Ehlebracht Associate Director of Financial Aid Financial Aid Manager at Curves for Women, Bank Teller and Customer Service Representative at First National Bank History Sean Flynn, Ph.D. Professor in the Department of History History He has been awarded the United Methodist Church General Board of Higher Education and Ministry Teaching Excellence Award and the Clarke Award for Teaching Excellence Award. He has written four books, including \"Without Reservation: Benjamin Reifel and American Indian Acculturation\" (Pierre: South Dakota Historical Society Press, 2018), a biography of South Dakota's only American Indian congressperson; and \"Chief, Marine Corps Warrior\" (2003), a military biography of Flynn's father, a decorated aviator and Korean War POW and one of the few pilots of American Indian descent to fly combat missions in World War II and Korea. Human Resources Carol Grode-Hanks, Ed.D. Human Resources Manager Human Resources I began my career teaching English, math, and social sciences to students in grades 7-12, a role I held for ten years. I then spent five years in the telecommunications industry, leading major software conversions and launching an in-house training “university” to support client development. In 2004, I joined Mitchell Technical College as Registrar. Over the years, I assumed a variety of roles—including Campus Management Systems, Curriculum Director, Dean of Faculty, and ultimately Vice President of Academics—focusing on campus management systems, curriculum development, and academic leadership. Information Technology Christopher Bernhardt Director of IT Information Technology Jonah Gates Database Administrator | Programmer Information Technology Juliet Hatmaker IT Senior Support Specialist Information Technology Learning Management System (LMS) Administrator and Computer Services Coordinator (St. Andrew's University) Alec Kulm Database Report Writer Information Technology Noor Sumaiya, M.S. IT Digital Support Technician Information Technology Fredel Thomas, MBA Vice President of Admissions, Marketing and Technology Admissions, Marketing and Communications, Information Technology Fredel started her career at DWU as director of the Kelly Center for Entrepreneurship, where she taught entrepreneurial leadership courses and served as a resource for regional businesses in South Dakota. She was named dean of admissions in 2015 and was promoted to vice president of admissions and marketing in 2018. As an extension to her work at DWU, Fredel served as chair of the Council on College Admissions in South Dakota, is a board member of the Dakota  Association for College Admission Counseling, serves on the South Dakota Freedom Scholarship Advisory Council, is an affiliate for Credo, a higher education consulting firm, and a frequent speaker for the National Small College Enrollment Conference. Prior to DWU, Fredel worked 12 years in the telecommunications and technology industry as a programmer, quality assurance officer, project manager and director of product management. She has served as a board member for the Weekend Snack Pack, the Abbott House, the Mitchell Area Chamber of Commerce, the Safe Place of Eastern South Dakota, and Avera Queen of Peace. She is active in her church where she leads youth group. Byron Warren Systems Administrator Information Technology Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Jessica Dollahon, DBA Assistant Director of the Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship | Director of the MBA Program | Assistant Professor of Management Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship, Business Essendant (Business Development Specialist & Consultant), Lagasse-Sweet (Vendor Coordinator), Multiple Co's (Insurance Agent) Diana Goldammer, Ed.D. Associate Professor | Director of the Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Business, Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Dr. Goldammer started her professional career as a high school English teacher. She moved into the private sector and worked in telecommunications and agribusiness. Here at DWU, Dr. Goldammer worked in public relations, went into student life in 2009, and in 2019 joined the business faculty. Library Laurie Langland, J.D. Archivist Library Hope Schulte Circulation and Interlibrary Loan Supervisor Library Angie Sewell, M.A. Serials | Cataloging | Acquisitions Librarian Library I began my career at the University of Sioux Falls, working at Mears Library. Since then, I’ve spent over 12 years in school libraries across the Midwest, including roles within the Sioux Falls School District, West Fargo School District, and South Sioux City School District. Lori Wehlander, M.S., M.Ed. Director of Library Resources | Teaching and Learning Specialist Library Compass/BHSSC (Eduction Learning Specialist), Huron School District (Director of Special Services), Iroquois and Carthage School Districts (Superintendent/Elementary Principal) Marketing and Communications Julie Brookbank, M.A. Associate Director of Communications Marketing and Communications Mitchell Technical College (Vice-President for Advancement, 2019-2021), Mitchell Technical College (Associate to the President, 2017-2019), Mitchell Technical College (Director of Marketing, 1995-2017), Mitchell Technical College (Public Information Specialist, 1991-1995) Jordan Glanzer Creative Content Developer Marketing and Communications Jan Larson, MBA, PCM Director of University Marketing and Communications Marketing and Communications Larson was previously employed at TrioTel Communications, Inc., a broadband provider based in Salem, for more than 10 years while holding positions as director of internal operations and as marketing supervisor. She worked for local and statewide political campaigns and as an intern for Sen. John Thune in Washington, D.C. She previously served as a board member of Mitchell’s First Circuit CASA, and currently serves as a board member for the Safe Place of Eastern South Dakota. She is a member of Mitchell’s Downtown First United Methodist Church. Chad Larson Graphic Design Specialist Marketing and Communications Fredel Thomas, MBA Vice President of Admissions, Marketing and Technology Admissions, Marketing and Communications, Information Technology Fredel started her career at DWU as director of the Kelly Center for Entrepreneurship, where she taught entrepreneurial leadership courses and served as a resource for regional businesses in South Dakota. She was named dean of admissions in 2015 and was promoted to vice president of admissions and marketing in 2018. As an extension to her work at DWU, Fredel served as chair of the Council on College Admissions in South Dakota, is a board member of the Dakota  Association for College Admission Counseling, serves on the South Dakota Freedom Scholarship Advisory Council, is an affiliate for Credo, a higher education consulting firm, and a frequent speaker for the National Small College Enrollment Conference. Prior to DWU, Fredel worked 12 years in the telecommunications and technology industry as a programmer, quality assurance officer, project manager and director of product management. She has served as a board member for the Weekend Snack Pack, the Abbott House, the Mitchell Area Chamber of Commerce, the Safe Place of Eastern South Dakota, and Avera Queen of Peace. She is active in her church where she leads youth group. Mathematics Mike Farney, Ph.D. Professor Emeritus, mathematics Mathematics Farney teaches courses in physics, mathematics and astronomy. His current work beyond the classroom takes him to local school districts many times each year to encourage the young to become involved in scientific research, mathematics research and engineering. Joan Lubben, Ph.D. Professor of Mathematics Mathematics Jacob Menix, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Mathematics Mathematics Ethan Semrad, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Mathematics Mathematics University of South Dakota - Graduate Teaching Assistant (2015-2017) | Robert F. Munroe Day School - Math/Science Teaching (2018-2019) | Tallahassee Community College - Adjunct Mathematics Instructor (2018-2019) | Florida State University - Graduate Teaching Assistant (2019-2024) | Wabash College - Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics (2024-2025) McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service Joel Allen, Ph.D. Professor of Religion and Philosophy | Director of the McGovern Center McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service, Religion Lambuth University (2008 – 2011) Associate Professor of Religion, Union College (2005-2008) Adjunct in Bible and History Music Erin Desmond, M.M.Ed. Associate Professor of Music | University Accompanist Music Previously, Before moving to South Dakota in 2010, she taught general and vocal music at Belvidere South Middle School, Belvidere, Ind., and taught vocal music at Willowcreek Middle School in Portage, Ind. She also acted aswas the Area One Representative for the Circle the State with Song Choral Festival, and was the assistant and accompanist for the Southlake Children’s Choir from 2005-2007. Presently, Desmond serves as the R&S chair for Junior High/Middle School Choirs for SD-ACDA. Clinton Desmond, DMA Department Chair | Director of Choral Activities Music Desmond has taught junior high and high school choir and has sung leading roles in opera and musical theatre. He debuted the role of Doctor Higgins in the 2005 world premiere performance and recording of Nancy Van de Vate’s “Where the Cross Is Made.” Corbin Kramer Performing Arts Talent Coordinator Admissions, Music, Theatre Jason Laczkoski Instructor of Instrumental Music Music Elizabeth Soladay Adjunct Instructor of Piano, Organ and Strings | LyricWood Orchestra Director Music Nursing Lori Bork, Ph.D., M.S.N., RN Associate Professor of Nursing Nursing Critical Care Nurse at Avera Health (1986–2011) | Nursing Faculty at Dakota Wesleyan University (2000–2015) | Nursing Program Chair at National American University (2015–2019) | Curriculum Consultant at Dakota Wesleyan University (2021–2025) | Nursing Informatics Specialist at Monument Health (2019–2026) MacKenzie Brandt, M.S.N., RN Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing BSN-RN at Avera McKennan in Sioux Falls within the women's and children's division for 6 years and counting! I’ve also served as a clinical adjunct in Pediatric and Maternal Health for multiple nursing programs for 4 years. Paige Gau, M.S.N., RN, CPN Associate Professor of Nursing Nursing Pediatric nurse at Sanford Children's Hospital since 2013, Clinical instructor since 2018 and Nursing Instructor at Southeast Technical College Wendy Helleloid Administrative Assistant Nursing Spent the last 24 years in the banking industry. Amy Hodge, M.S.N., RN, CNP, PMHNP-BC Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing Angela Klumb, B.S.N., RN Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing 1 summer Certified Staff Assistant Omaha Med Center Neurology Unit 2008, 1 year RN Bryan Health LGH 2009, 7 years RN Avera Queen of Peace Hospital- I still work shifts as PRN, 7 years RN Clinic Supervisor Avera Medical Group Dermatology, Current Dakota Wesleyan Nursing Instructor Nathan Leonard, M.S.N., RN Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing Kassie Marek, M.S.N., RN Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing Registered Nurse for 22 years with experience across a wide range of specialties, including bedside nursing in NICU, Maternal-Fetal Medicine, Labor & Delivery, Pediatrics, and Emergency Medicine. Served as Director of Nursing in both the Emergency Department and Intensive Care Unit. Additionally, taught as a Nursing Instructor for six years in both classroom and clinical settings. Stacey Patzlaff, M.S.N., RN, OCN Professor of Nursing Nursing I have an extensive background in Oncology and Medical-Surgical nursing, with additional experience in Dialysis and the ICU. Breanna Price, B.S.N., RN Instructor of Nursing Nursing Registered Nurse since 2017 with travel nursing experience from 2018–2026. Sarah Raml, M.S.N., M.A., RN Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing Labor and Delivery Nurse at Sanford Health (2005–2024) Penny Tilton, DNP, M.S.N., RN Associate Professor of Nursing | Dean of the Donna Starr Christen College of Healthcare, Fitness and Sciences | Administrative Chair of Nursing Nursing Before coming to Dakota Wesleyan University, I taught nursing at SDSU for 6 years. Physical Plant Kevin Adams Director of Physical Plant Physical Plant Menards department manager 18 years Taylor Baldwin Custodial Maintenance Physical Plant Sandy Byrd Custodian Physical Plant Kathy Gardner Custodian Physical Plant Jeff Harris Maintenance Technician Physical Plant Elwin Hohn Custodian Physical Plant Eric Lofgren Maintenance Technician Physical Plant Ronald Pavlin Custodian Physical Plant Ashlee Reck Custodian Physical Plant D'Andra Rogers Custodian Physical Plant Louie Schoenfelder Associate Physical Plant Director Physical Plant Auto/diesel mechanic, dairy farmer Brian Voorhees Custodian Physical Plant President Emily George Executive Administrative Assistant President, Provost and Academic Affairs Dan Kittle, Ph.D. President President Served in Student Affairs at Michigan State University, 16 years at Wartburg College; served in faculty development, community engagement, service-learning, as well as served as the Assistant to the President for Strategic Initiatives and as the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students. Provost and Academic Affairs Emily George Executive Administrative Assistant President, Provost and Academic Affairs Ryan Glidden, Ed.D. Instructional Designer Provost and Academic Affairs I've worked as an Instructional Designer since 2016. Prior to that I had roles in academic advising, admissions, and campus events. Recently, I started looking at informal learning spaces as a way to create social connections and develop a sense of belonging in third spaces, aiding in student retention. Mickie Metzinger, Ph.D. Provost Provost and Academic Affairs University of Saint Mary, Provost (2017 - 2026) | Presentation College, Vice President for Academics (1999 - 2017) | Cresbard School District, Business Teacher (1996-1999) | Van Meter School District, K-6 Computer Teacher, (1994-1995) Melissa Weber, Ed.D. Associate Dean of Strategic Initiatives | Associate Professor of Education | Master of Arts in Education Director Education, Provost and Academic Affairs Canistota School District (ELA Teacher, Librarian, Assistant Principal, Curriculum Director) from 2007-2018; Bridgewater School District (ELA Teacher) from 2005-2007 Registrar Crystal Luna, M.Ed. Assistant Registrar Registrar Anderson University (Director of Educational Support Services, and Assistant Director of Adult Learning), MidAmerica Nazarene University (Academic Coordinator for Adults in MHR program) Molly Manchester, MME Registrar Registrar 5th-12th Grade Band Director, 7th-12th Grade Choir Director Caitlin Ostbye, MSAL, CSCS Associate Registrar | Assistant Strength and Conditioning Coach | Assistant Track and Field Coach Registrar, Athletics Graduate Assistant for Track and Field and Strength and Conditioning at Augustana University (2025), Student Strength and Conditioning Assistant - Northwestern College (2020-2024), Strength and Conditioning Intern at University of North Carolina Chapel Hill (2023) Religion Joel Allen, Ph.D. Professor of Religion and Philosophy | Director of the McGovern Center McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service, Religion Lambuth University (2008 – 2011) Associate Professor of Religion, Union College (2005-2008) Adjunct in Bible and History Sport Exercise and Wellness Kyle Hobbs, M.Ed. Assistant Professor of Sport, Exercise and Wellness Sport Exercise and Wellness Dakota Wesleyan University (Head Strength and Conditioning Coach and Adjunct Professor of Sport, Exercise and Wellness), University of Delaware (Strength and Conditioning Assistant Coach), University of Georgia (Georgia Football Strength and Conditioning Coach) Student Support Services Caleb Crist, MBA Student Success Adviser Student Support Services Union Lumber/Ace Hardware - Marysville, C.A. (2017-2020) | Karl's TV and Appliance - Mitchell, S.D. (Summer 2022) | Vantage Point Solutions - Mitchell, S.D. (2023-2025) Tiffany Ellis, M.A. Academic Success Coordinator Student Support Services Fuller Center for Housing (Global Builders Program Manager & Bike Adventure Trip Leader) | Russell Media (Digital Marketing Account Manager) | Ball State University (Assistant Lecturer of ESL) | Fulbright Student Program (English Teaching Assistant (North Macedonia '12-'13)) | Ball State University (Graduate Assistant (ESL Instructor)) Luke Loudenburg, M.Ed. Student Success Adviser Student Support Services Kelli Mueller, M.Ed. Office of Disability Services Coordinator | Student Success Adviser Student Support Services Mitchell School District (7th/8th grade science instructor) Jodi Wilson, M.S.Ed. Director of TRIO Student Support Services Third Grade Teacher (Longfellow Elementary), Computer Teacher (John Paul II Elementary) and Contract Manager (FARR Technologies) Theatre Corbin Kramer Performing Arts Talent Coordinator Admissions, Music, Theatre Dan Miller, MFA Professor of Theatre | Chair of the Ron and Sheilah Gates Department of Theatre Theatre Associate Professor of Theatre (Tenured) and Director of Theatre, Dakota Wesleyan University, 2014 - Present; Assistant Professor of Comm. / Theatre, Director of Theatre, Dakota Wesleyan University, 2006 - 2014; Box Office Manager, New Harmony Theatre (LORT), New Harmony, IN, 2006; Adjunct Theatre Instructor of Theatre, University of Southern Indiana, Evansville, IN; Lecturer of Drama, University of Evansville, Evansville, IN; Artistic Managing Director Evansville Civic Theatre Evansville, IN Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: The best way to determine whether DWU is the place for you is to visit. Schedule a Visit Request Information Apply for Free Visit Us 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy"
