rements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Majors & Minors Explore Our  Many Programs All All Majors Minors Mitchell Tech Partnership Preprofessional Track All All Majors Minors Mitchell Tech Partnership Preprofessional Track Grid List Accounting Explore the world of finance with the confidence to oversee the financial needs of business and accounting firms. Explore Major Agriculture Business Use your business knowledge in an ag-related career. Finance, insurance, commodity marketing and farm/ranch management are just a few of the areas where business and ag intersect. Explore Mitchell Tech Partnership Allied Health Be ready for the positions that comprise over half the jobs in healthcare today, such as medical technologist, occupational therapist or physical therapist. Explore Minor Architecture and Design Applying design concepts to interior and exterior spaces using today’s most advanced software and technology. Form follows function in our Architecture and Design program. Explore Mitchell Tech Partnership Athletic Training An exciting career in sports healthcare and rehabilitation, using hands-on learning experiences, is waiting for you in our Master’s in Athletic Training program. Explore Major Behavioral Sciences Explore the vast universe of human behavior. Explore Major Minor Biochemistry Explore the living things around you, while you investigate the complexity of life processes in animals and plants. Explore Major Biology Sequence DNA or discover a new spider species. Study biology with professors with backgrounds spanning from plant ecology to human immune systems. Explore Major Minor Business Administration As a business administration major at DWU, you’ll prepare for limitless career choices in the professional world. Explore Major Minor Chemistry If problem solving is your thing, you'll fit right in at DWU. As a chemistry major, you’ll study the elements that make up our world, including the composition, behavior and chemical change of matter. Explore Major Minor Christian Leadership A degree in Christian leadership will help you impact a faith community and find satisfaction in a life of service and discipleship. Explore Major Minor Communication Excellent communication skills are sought by every employer, and it’s a true professional who elevates the skill of communicating to an art. Explore Major Minor Computer Information Systems Like computers? Let’s go! Learn programming, systems analysis, and data management — connecting tech with business strategy. Explore Major Construction Management A successful construction management career depends on a strong background in construction and a good business sense. This combination will help you build a great career. Explore Mitchell Tech Partnership Creative Writing Do you aspire to write fiction, poetry or screenplays? A minor in creative writing will give you a solid foundation in English so you can pursue being a professional creative writer. Explore Minor Criminal Justice Discover ways to use your talents for law, law enforcement, juvenile support, corrections, court reporting or many other ways that are a part of the United States legal system. Explore Major Minor Digital Media and Design The ever-growing technology industry needs talented people like you to create and design digital elements for countless applications. Explore Major Education You can have a profound impact on the next generation when you enroll in an education program at DWU. Explore Major English Ready to read, write, think and explore? An English major prepares you to think, analyze and explain language, and is an excellent fit for a communication or teaching career. Explore Major English Literature Immerse yourself in the written word. Explore cultures and experiences through European, British and American authors. Explore Minor Entrepreneurial Leadership Entrepreneur is not a job title – it’s a way of thinking. Entrepreneurship involves innovation, curiosity and risk. Explore Major Minor Exercise Science Exercising and maintaining a healthy body takes motivation and hard work. Use your passion for gym time with an exercise science degree from DWU. Explore Major Minor Fitness and Sport Management From personal trainer to team or facility management to the front office of a professional athletic team, your unique skill set combining business, communication and sports will make you a winner. Explore Major General Studies Take a trip down a liberal arts path with a major in general studies. Improve your leadership and communication skills, cultivate roots in service and stewardship, and prepare for a variety of careers that make a difference in the world. Explore Major History Pursue the intricacies of history at DWU. Through your exploration, your critical thinking skills will be tested as you read, review, research and write. Explore Major Minor Mathematics Develop your love for math. Learn the skills to harness theories, understand technology application, and present research with confidence. Explore Major Minor Music Join Dakota Wesleyan’s musical family as a vocalist or instrumentalist. Study and perform whether you are a major, a minor or you just need a little bit more music in your life. Explore Major Minor Music Management and Marketing Make music your career and your business. Our Music Management and Marketing major prepares you to manage artists, plan events, and market music in a rapidly changing industry. Explore Major Music Ministry Combine faith and music in meaningful ways. Our Music Ministry major educates students to lead worship, direct choirs and ensembles, and use music to engage and uplift communities. Explore Major Nursing Our nursing programs are among the best in the region. As a nursing student, you will learn and grow within a community of support. Explore Major Political Science Embrace your interest in politics. Pursue a career in law, government or education with a minor in political science. Explore Minor Pre-Law Is a career in law in your future? DWU will help you prepare. Our law school-bound students have graduated with degrees as diverse as accounting, business, communication, criminal justice and psychology. Explore Preprofessional Track Pre-Medicine and Related Health Professions Pursuing a degree in medicine or another health profession after Dakota Wesleyan? Our advantage is the faculty. Explore Preprofessional Track Pre-Physical Therapy Help sick or injured people improve their mobility and manage pain. Rehabilitate someone who has been injured or be an advocate for those with chronic conditions. Explore Preprofessional Track Pre-Theology Called to ministry, and want to become an ordained pastor? Pre-theology coursework at Dakota Wesleyan University will help guide you on your path to seminary. Explore Preprofessional Track Psychology Our psychology major will take you on an exploration of human behavior from biological, behavioral, cognitive, social and cultural viewpoints. Explore Major Minor Sociology Learn how to understand human dynamics related to family, religion, economics, government and education. Explore Minor Sports Management Become a valuable player in any sports organization and embrace your love of athletics. Explore Minor Theatre Turn your love for acting, storytelling, and performance into a theatre career, either on stage or behind the scenes. Explore Major Minor Wildlife Management Embrace an outdoor lifestyle and promote environmental stewardship with a degree in Wildlife Management. Explore Major Minor Accounting Agriculture Business Allied Health Architecture and Design Athletic Training Behavioral Sciences Biochemistry Biology Business Administration Chemistry Christian Leadership Communication Computer Information Systems Construction Management Creative Writing Criminal Justice Digital Media and Design Education English English Literature Entrepreneurial Leadership Exercise Science Fitness and Sport Management General Studies History Mathematics Music Music Management and Marketing Music Ministry Nursing Political Science Pre-Law Pre-Medicine and Related Health Professions Pre-Physical Therapy Pre-Theology Psychology Sociology Sports Management Theatre Wildlife Management What major should I choose if I'm undecided? Our Academic and Career Services Center is here to help you find and use your strengths, connect your talents with your educational goals and give you the clarity and focus you need to\n        succeed well after you graduate from DWU. Learn More Can’t find what you are dreaming of? Not to worry. There is always the option to work toward creating a major that fits you. Our advisers will get to know you and your goals to create a major tailored to your needs. Learn More I'm a Select your student category High School Student College graduate looking at master's degrees Adult looking to complete my degree Pastor looking for Practical Church Leadership program Professional looking for MBA degree Teacher looking for M.Ed. degree Professional looking for a certificate Nurse looking to complete my degree Other Please mail information about Dakota Wesleyan University. Request Information Request more information Complete the form to request more information from Dakota Wesleyan University. Student Category High School Student High School Student College graduate looking for MBA Degree College graduate looking for M.Ed. Degree College graduate looking for MAT Degree Adult looking to complete my degree Pastor looking for Practical Church Leadership program Professional looking for MBA degree Teacher looking for M.Ed. degree Professional looking for a certificate Nurse looking to complete my degree Other First Name * Last Name * Email * Address * Apt / Suite # City * State * Alabama --Select-- Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Guam Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Puerto Rico Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Virgin Islands Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyo