equirements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Mitchell Scholars Program Advancing Education Together A transformative $33 million donation has been made to the Mitchell community with the explicit goal of elevating local education and making Mitchell, South Dakota, the premier community for\n        education. Gifted by Roger and Vicki Musick, the funds are earmarked as two $15 million endowments, one for the Mitchell Public School District and one for Dakota Wesleyan University, launching a new\n        era of opportunity for students, educators and administrators. The remaining $3 million is being presented to the institutions as immediate seed money to launch these programs without delay. Pathway to Higher Education “This donation is based on the belief that nothing is more important than great educators. These funds are intended to provide comprehensive scholarships for all educators and\n        administrators in the Mitchell Public School District to pursue master's degrees and professional development from DWU. It will also establish scholarships for graduates of Mitchell\n        High School, with additional scholarships provided for high school juniors and seniors who receive free or reduced lunch to take DWU courses, creating a vital and affordable pathway to\n        higher education.” - Roger Musick With this incredible gift, the DWU Musick Endowment Fund has been created to support the Mitchell Scholars Program. Educating Teachers Teachers in the Mitchell Public School District will have an opportuntity to earn a Master of Arts in Education degree tuition free from DWU. With five degree options available, Mitchell\n        teachers will have the ability to select a degree option that fits their goals. Additionally, Dakota Wesleyan Unviersity will provide the Mitchell School District with Teachers' Aides to support teachers in the classroom. Master's Degrees for Mitchell Teachers Empowering Mitchell Public Schools “This gift will transform the opportunities we can offer our Mitchell Public School students, both now and for generations to come. Roger and Vicki’s generosity is a powerful\n        expression of faith in our schools, and in the young people, families and educators who make this community strong. Their vision recognizes that when we invest in early learning, grow\n        after-school opportunities and help our teachers reach their fullest potential, we are setting the stage for lifelong success. This is more than a donation. This is the\n        beginning of a brighter future for all of Mitchell.\" - Dr. Joe Childs, Superintendent of Mitchell School District Managed via the newly formed Mitchell Public Schools Foundation for Academic Excellence, the endowment will underwrite: A full-day no-cost Begindergarten program (for children not quite ready for kindergarten) Expansive, free after-school programs at all district elementary schools Enrichment offerings, additional tutors and support services These enhancements are intended to supplement, not replace, existing public funding. Mitchell School District Mitchell High School Students Mitchell High School students have the unique opportunity to continue their education close to home. The Bridge Program offers Mitchell students a chance to take\n        college courses and earn college credit while in high school. Additionally, MHS graduates will receive special scholarship award and personalized support to make the transition to DWU smooth\n        and affordable. MHS Bridge Program MHS Scholarship Opportunities Bridge Program DWU On-Campus Visit Returning Mitchell Students At Dakota Wesleyan, students are more than just a number, and, compared to other colleges in South Dakota, students are supported and inspired to make a difference. Mitchell High School graduates who have started their college journey elsewhere and want to transfer to DWU, will be able to take advantage of a $2,500 transfer\n        scholarship designed to make finishing a bachelor's degree close to home affordable and seamless. MHS Transfer Students Making Mitchell Home \"This donation is a powerful investment in the future of Mitchell, giving every student the opportunity to succeed. But this is just the beginning. By working together, the people of Mitchell\n        can ensure the city becomes a beacon for young families and a place where every child can thrive.\" - Roger Musick With free after-school programs, free master's degrees and multiple scholarship opportunities, Mitchell, South Dakota, is THE community for living and working. About Mitchell In the News Thank you to our local and regional media partners for providing coverage of this transformational gift. Subscriptions may be required to access news links\n        below. Mitchell Republic : LIVESTREAM: DWU and Mitchell Public Schools\n        announcement Mitchell Republic : Roger, Vicki Musick\n        gifts $33 million in 'historic' donation to Mitchell Public Schools, Dakota Wesleyan Dakota News Now : $33 million donation made for Mitchell education\n        advancements KELOLAND News : $33 million gift to change Mitchell education forever South Dakota Public Broadcasting : Mitchell School District,\n        DWU receive 'transformative' gift of $33M KOTA : $33 Million Gift Transforms Education in Mitchell, SD Mitchell Republic : Hagen: Big donation makes for Mitchell's\n        biggest story ever Philanthropy News Digest : Mitchell School District, Dakota Wesleyan\n        receive $33 million Mitchell Republic : ' Wonderful’ new KERNELS\n        after school program welcomes first batch of students Mitchell Republic : When can we\n        get started?’ Free master’s degrees incoming for Mitchell School District teachers Mitchell Republic : Musick endowment adds new dimension to\n        Mitchell’s community appeal Mitchell Now : $30M Musick Endowment Strengthens Education, Community\n        Appeal DWU News : DWU appoints Education professor to new position Mitchell Republic : Kittle: What does it mean for Dakota Wesleyan\n        University SD Searchlight : Belief in education’s role\n        in community drove $33 million gift, donor says Pierre Capital Journal : Mitchell man talks\n        about his motivation for donating to local schools and university Making Mitchell, South Dakota, the Premier Community for Education View larger image: MG_8669.jpg View larger image: MG_8678.jpg View larger image: MG_8671.jpg View larger image: MG_8723.jpg View larger image: MG_8722.jpg View larger image: MG_8703.jpg View larger image: MG_8760.jpg View larger image: MG_8713.jpg View larger image: MG_8736.jpg View larger image: MG_8710.jpg View larger image: MG_8717.jpg View larger image: MG_8673.jpg Mitchell Scholars Program Quick Links: Mitchell Teachers Mitchell School District MHS Bridge Program MHS Scholarship Opportunities MHS Transfer Students About Mitchell Questions? Just email us or give us a call. Phone: (605) 995-2650 Email: admissions@dwu.edu Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
