ements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Tuition & Fees We can help make a DWU education possible for you EVERY student receives some form of financial aid. On average,\n        Wesleyan students receive $24,000 in financial aid. That amount includes scholarships, grants and loans. \" When I transferred to DWU from a state school, I found that my out-of-pocket costs were about the same, even though I expected DWU to cost a lot more. Wesleyan offers a lot of scholarships, making my actual cost very manageable. All of my credits were accepted by DWU, so I didn’t lose anything when I transferred. Plus, I feel like I’m getting a higher quality education at DWU. \" - Codi, accounting major 2026-27 Costs Tuition costs are based on 12-16 credit hours per semester. Tuition: $33,600 Student Services and Activities: $640 Technology Fee: $880 Living Expenses: $9,000 Total*: $44,120 *These costs are based on 12-16 credit hours per semester and the average living expenses (room and meal plan). Actual fees may vary. This amount does not include books, travel\n                or personal expenses. Rewarding Your Strengths. Students who apply and are accepted for admission will be automatically considered for academic scholarships based on their high school GPA. Transfer students are\n        awarded an academic scholarship based on their college GPA. Visit with an admissions counselor for more\n        details. High school seniors have an opportunity to compete for DWU’s top scholarships – the Randall Scholarship\n        or the Presidential Leadership Scholarship – at our competitive scholarship days. We offer two scholarship days, one in\n        the fall and one in the spring . Many scholarships are available, and numerous loan and grant programs can also supplement the cost. DWU’s experienced team is dedicated to making the\n        financial aid process work for each student. Scholarships and Financial Aid Information Net Price Calculator Questions? Please email us or give us a call. Phone: (605) 995-2650 Email: admissions@dwu.edu Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
