the requirements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin New Student Registration You’re one step closer to being a DWU student We are excited to begin the process of registration with you. We make it simple and are here to help. New Student Registration Day Please fill out the form below to schedule your new student on-campus registration day, where you will register for classes, meet with your advisor, and get your official student ID. New Student Registration Day Events Friday, April 9, 2027 (afternoon) Sign-up deadline: April 2nd. Friday, April 23, 2027 (afternoon) Sign-up deadline: April 16th. Friday, May 14, 2027 (morning) Sign-up deadline: May 7th. Friday, June 11, 2027 (morning) Sign-up deadline: June 4th. New Student Registration Day Schedule Morning Session 8:30 am - Check-in (Sherman Center) 9:00 am - Welcome & First Year Tips 9:30 am - Noon - Student Advising Meetings & Completing Registration Checklist Afternoon Session 1:00 pm - Check-in (Sherman Center) 1:30 pm - Welcome & First Year Tips 2:00 pm - 4:30 pm - Student Advising Meetings & Completing Registration Checklist During Your New Student Registration Day, You Will Meet with financial aid and business offices to discuss scholarships, loans, and payment plan options. Meet with the campus nurse to discuss any health requirements. Take your student ID picture and receive your campus mailbox and email address. Receive your class schedule and meet with an advisor to learn how your class schedule fits into your four-year plan of study. Things to Know A $200 enrollment confirmation fee is due on the day of registration if you have not already paid. Download the helpful DWU Admissions Checklist to make sure you are completing all required tasks. If you are a transfer student or have previous college or dual credits, your official transcripts must be sent to DWU two weeks before Registration Day so they can be evaluated in time\n        for advising. New students must apply for admission and receive official notification of acceptance to Dakota Wesleyan University before signing up for a registration day. All new students must register\n        for fall semester classes before the start of the semester. Please Choose a Registration Option: --Select One-- --Select One-- Friday April 9th (afternoon) Friday April 23rd (afternoon) Friday May 14th (morning) Friday June 11th (morning) Virtual (your counselor will reach out to schedule) First Name: Last Name: Email: Mailing Address: City: State/Province: --Select One-- --Select One-- Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District Of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Alberta British Columbia Manitoba New Brunswick Newfoundland and Labrador Nova Scotia Ontario Prince Edward Island Quebec Saskatchewan Northwest Territories Nunavut Yukon Outside US and Canada ZIP/Postal Code: Home Phone: Cell Phone Number (with area code): Who is Coming with You?: Intended Major: --- Please Select One --- --- Please Select One --- Undecided Accounting Ag Business Architecture and Design Athletic Training Behavioral Sciences Biochemistry Biology Biology Education Business Administration Business Sports Management Chemistry Christian Leadership Communication Computer Information Systems Construction Management Criminal Justice Digital Media & Design Elementary Education English English Education Entrepreneurial Leadership Exercise Science Finance Fitness & Sport Management General Science Graphic Design History History Education Management Mathematics Mathematics Education Music Music Education Music Management & Marketing Music Ministry Nonprofit Administration Nursing Pre-dental Pre-law Pre-med Pre-physical therapy Pre-theology Psychology Special Education Theatre Web Design Wildlife Management Secondary Major / Minor: --- Please Select One --- --- Please Select One --- Undecided Accounting Ag Business Architecture and Design Athletic Training Behavioral Sciences Biochemistry Biology Biology Education Business Administration Business Sports Management Chemistry Christian Leadership Communication Computer Information Systems Construction Management Criminal Justice Design & Architecture Digital Media & Design Elementary Education English English Education Entrepreneurial Leadership Exercise Science Finance Fitness & Sport Management General Science Graphic Design History History Education Management Mathematics Mathematics Education Music Music Education Nonprofit Administration Nursing Pre-dental Pre-law Pre-med Pre-physical therapy Pre-theology Psychology Religious Studies Special Education Theatre Web Design Wildlife Management Parent is a DWU alumna/us: Yes Yes No If yes, please list parent name: Have you taken any AP classes or college classes?: Yes Yes No If yes, please have official transcripts sent to DWU and bring the list of courses taken with you on your new student registration day. Please list any current or past AP/College courses you have taken and where you took them from? (i.e. Biology 101 - Dakota Wesleyan University): Questions? Please email us or give us a call. 605-995-2650 admissions@dwu.edu Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Libr