      "title": "DWU",
      "description": "DWU | Transfer Students Skip to main content Search the site Search Athletics Performing Arts Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Visit Give Apply Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 40 majors and minors. Graduate & Online Explore on-campus and online graduate programs. A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Please Select... A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Apply for Free Begin an amazing new chapter in your life. Admission Requirements You belong at DWU. Take a look at the requirements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Transfer to DWU Is it time to make a change? Don't settle. You don’t have to settle for a college experience that isn’t working. Transferring to Dakota Wesleyan University means personalized support, an\n        easy credit transfer process, and scholarship opportunities that make finishing your degree more affordable than you imagined. Take the next step. Apply for FREE. Apply Now Why Transfer to DWU? You will be more than just a number. Our faculty will guide and support you during your college experience. DWU is different\n        than large state universities. With small class sizes, personal attention and over 40 academic programs, you'll thrive at DWU. 12:1 Student-to-Faculty Ratio 96% of graduates are employed or in grad school 100% job placement for nursing and education graduates Scholarship opportunities 30 clubs + 18 athletic teams Transferring to another college shouldn't be stressful. At DWU, we'll make this process a smooth transition for you and your family. Need more\n        information before applying? Connect with us! Let's Connect “I transferred to DWU because I wanted to be in the best nursing program in the state and the chance to compete on the track team. At DWU, you’re never just another number –\n        the whole campus community truly cares about you and makes you feel at home.\" - Will Requirements for Transfer Apply for Free In order to be accepted to DWU: You must have a cumulative GPA of 2.0 from a previous college/university. You must be in good standing with all previous institutions. Complete the FREE application. All on-campus, full-time students get a scholarship. That includes transfer students! An official DWU application must be submitted to the admissions office. There is no application\n        fee! Ready to apply ? Complete the DWU undergraduate\n        application now . Apply Now Submit College Transcripts College Transcripts You may submit unofficial transcripts for acceptance to DWU. However, official transcripts, from all previous colleges, universities, professional and\n        vocational schools, and technical schools must be submitted once your final grades have been posted. Official transcripts with the original seal and\n        signature must be sent directly from the originating institutions to the DWU Admissions Office. Any opened envelopes, scans, or copies of these transcripts will be considered\n        unofficial. High School Transcripts If you have less than one year of college coursework completed, high school transcripts will need to be submitted for acceptance. Once all of your transcripts have been submitted, your file will then be reviewed for acceptance. Upon completion of the review, you will be notified of your acceptance status by DWU. Apply for Financial Aid We encourage you to complete your FAFSA with our\n        school code (003461). The sooner we have your FAFSA, the sooner we can provide you with an estimate of your financial assistance. DWU School Code = 003461 FASFA Pay Enrollment Confirmation Submit a $200 enrollment confirmation. You can pay in person (cash, check or credit card), by phone or online. Business Office Dakota Wesleyan University 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 If you have any questions about paying, connect with\n        our accounts receivable specialist. Pay Enrollment Confirmation Grid List Kerri Fahey Accounts Receivable Specialist Abra Auto Body & Glass, Palace Builders, Guidehouse Kerri Fahey Accounts Receivable Specialist Abra Auto Body & Glass, Palace Builders, Guidehouse Show More Complete Online Housing Form Please fill out the online housing form so we\n        can connect you with your living arrangements. Housing Form Submit Mandatory Health Forms Complete your health forms . Your DWU admissions counselor will\n        help you with this. Health Forms Register for Courses After you have been accepted to DWU, completed your FAFSA and paid your deposit, it’s time to register for\n        classes . Register for Classes Need help keeping track of everything? Download the Transfer Student Checklist to help\n        with the process. Transfer Checklist Are you a Mitchell High School graduate? It’s never too late to find a college that truly feels like home. Transfer to DWU and take advantage of the new Mitchell Scholarship created\n        just for you. MHS Transfer Students Transfer Student FAQs What is DWU’s definition of a transfer? A transfer student is anyone applying for admission to Dakota Wesleyan University who attended a\n        college or university after high school graduation. If you are completing college courses while in high school, you are considered a freshman and not a transfer student. Will I be accepted to DWU? In order to be accepted to DWU: You must have a cumulative GPA of 2.0 from a previous college/university. You must be in good standing with all previous institutions. If you have not completed one full year at a college or university, you must have a 2.0 high school GPA. Do I need to provide my high school transcripts? Your DWU transfer coordinator will\n        inform you if your high school transcript is needed. What deadlines does DWU have for incoming students? Priority deadline for financial aid is Feb. 1. This includes the completion and submission of\n        your FAFSA . What steps do I need to take if I’m an athlete? If the coaching staff has already contacted you, they likely will have directed you to apply and contact your transfer coordinator. If you have not been contacted, we encourage you to fill out a questionnaire letting us know which sport you are interested in participating in.\n        You can access the form here . It is also essential that you request your release from your current institution to comply with NAIA recruitment efforts. The coaching staff will work\n        with you on this matter, as well as walking you through the NAIA registration process. If you have questions about who to contact or any general athletic questions, please contact the\n        athletic department at 605-995-2112 . Will my credits transfer in to DWU? If so, how many? The DWU registrar will evaluate your transcript(s). If you are transferring from a community or technical college, you will receive up to 60 transferring credits from your respective\n                institution. If you are transferring from a four-year university, you will receive as many credits as approved by the DWU registrar. DWU will not accept developmental credits. Any questions or concerns regarding whether a credit will be transferred to DWU will be at the discretion of the registrar and the department\n                chair. What scholarships are available through DWU? Academic scholarships are available to you based on your previous GPA. In order to qualify, you must have a minimum GPA of 2.0. 4.0 GPA: $16,000 3.75 - 3.99 GPA: $14,750 2.50 - 3.74 GPA: $13,750 3.00 - 3.49 GPA: $13,000 2.99 or below: $10,000 Athletic, Performing Arts, Student Ministry, and eSports scholarships are also available. Scholarship amounts are determined by coaches and\n        directors. Members of the Phi Theta Kappa Honor Chapter may qualify for an additional scholarship up to $2,000. Be sure to submit your proof of membership to your admissions\n        counselor. Members of the United Methodist Church also qualify for a $1,000 annual scholarship. Additional outside scholarships are available to all students. How much will it cost to attend DWU? Does it change if I’m from out of state? There is no difference in cost whether you are from\n        South Dakota or from elsewhere. For tuition costs and other expenses, please visit our tuition and fees page . I’m accepted! Now what do I need to do? Congratulations on your acceptance, and welcome to the DWU family! DWU will review any outstanding documents so you can register for classes. When you have registered for classes, we will also need your financial aid promissory\n        note, medical records, athletic letter of intent (for student-athletes) and any other paperwork requested by DWU. You should also contact the business office to set up billing information and\n        payment plans. Need help keeping track of everything? Download the Transfer Student Checklist to help with the process! Transfer Checklist Partner Institutions DWU has standing agreements with community and technical colleges to make the transfer process easier. These agreements allow you to complete a bachelor’s\n        degree at DWU using credit earned in specific programs at other institutions. Often, the degree or program completed at your prior institution will become your minor at DWU. In other\n        instances, the agreement allows the application of those prior courses as part of your DWU major. Our partnering institutions and the corresponding programs are listed below. If you find your current school and/or program is not listed, this does\n        not mean your credits will not be accepted. For all incoming students, a course-by-course transcript evaluation will be completed by the registrar’s office. Mitchell Technical College (Mitchell, SD) DWU and Mitchell Tech DWU and Mitchell Tech have a long-standing partnership in helping students reach their goals. From taking programs at both DWU and Mitchell Tech at the same time to\n        transferring from Mitchell Tech when you are done with your associate degree, you can expect a smooth and hassle-free process. Programs that qualify: Accounting Agricultural Business Agronomy Animal Science Architectural Design and Building Construction Culinary Academy Human Services ( Criminal Justice , Psychology ) Precision Ag Technology Northeast Community College (Norfolk, NE) Northeast Community College grads make great Tigers! We promise to work with you to transfer your credits and to make the transition as easy as possible. DWU and\n        NECC have partnered to provide a hassle-free transfer process to you can complete your bachelor's degree quickly and affordably. Programs that qualify: Accounting Master's in Athletic Training Business Administration Criminal Justice (Corrections and Law\n                Enforcement) Elementary Education Western Dakota Tech (Rapid City, SD) Programs that qualify: Accounting Business Management & Marketing Criminal Justice Lake Area Technical College (Watertown, SD) Programs that qualify: Physical Therapist Assistant Southeast Tech (Sioux Falls, SD) Programs that qualify: Accounting Business Administration Digital Media Production Technology Marketing Design\n                Technology Law Enforcement\n                Science Questions? Please email us or give us a call. 605-995-2650 admissions@dwu.edu Let's Connect Apply Now Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
