      "title": "DWU",
      "description": "DWU | Student Services Skip to main content Search the site Search Athletics Performing Arts Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Visit Give Apply Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 40 majors and minors. Graduate & Online Explore on-campus and online graduate programs. A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Please Select... A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Apply for Free Begin an amazing new chapter in your life. Admission Requirements You belong at DWU. Take a look at the requirements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Student Services We are here for you If you are away from home for the first time, you\n        might not know what to do when you have a health issue. Because we care about all aspects of your health: physical, mental and spiritual, there are different places on campus where you can go for your different needs. We are here for you Physical Health and Wellness Mental Health Spiritual Health Campus Worship Services Academic Assistance IT Services Physical Health and Wellness We have a registered nurse available to help you with your health and wellness needs. Just visit Student Health Services on the lower level of the Rollins Campus\n        Center. If you need a physician or require more immediate medical attention, you may be referred to a local doctor if necessary. In an emergency, the Avera Queen of Peace\n        Emergency Room is nearby. Mandatory Health Forms Complete the Student Health Form on TigerGO . Dakota Wesleyan University requires that all full-time students carrying 12 or more credit hours must have a billable major medical insurance policy. Check\n                with your individual policy provider for details about your coverage. Submit a photocopy of your medical insurance card on TigerGo . Submit an official copy of your completed immunization record to the DWU Campus Nurse: Dakota Wesleyan University Campus Nurse 1200 W. University Ave., Box 926 Mitchell, SD 57301 Scan and email as a PDF file to dwunurse@dwu.edu . Submit a Physical Evaluation form . See Immunization Requirements See Common Illnesses For your ongoing wellness activity, the DWU/Avera Sports and Wellness Complex is available 24/7. All full-time students are automatically members of the GreatLIFE,\n        which means you can use other GreatLIFE facilities if you travel. The 200-meter track is available for running and walking year round. Check out other DWU Facilities Mental Health We offer on-campus counseling services with a trained and licensed counselor here to help you sort through the issues that often come up in a student’s life:\n        relationships, adjusting to campus life, academic struggles, addiction, stress and mental health issues—whatever you need to talk about. All sessions\n        are free of charge and completely confidential. Your clinical file is not a part of your academic records, and it is protected under HIPAA . Office hours are Monday-Friday from 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Drop-ins are welcomed and encouraged! Scheduled appointments are also available. If you prefer, the campus counselor can provide referrals for licensed, outpatient therapists in the Mitchell community. Outpatient therapy services in the\n        community are not covered by Dakota Wesleyan University, and therefore, at the student’s own expense. Grid List Kimberly Lienemann, M.A., LPC-MH, QMHP Campus Counselor I started working in the Behavioral Health field 30 years ago, and I became a licensed therapist in 2004 in Nebraska. The majority of my career was spent in residential, long term, treatment centers for adolescents and adults including four years on an acute psychiatric unit of a hospital in Omaha. I held a variety of clinical supervisory and staff training positions during my years in residential. I started working in private practice in 2016. Licensed Professional Counselor - Mental Health (LPC-MH) South Dakota 2018 - Current. Kimberly Lienemann, M.A., LPC-MH, QMHP Campus Counselor I started working in the Behavioral Health field 30 years ago, and I became a licensed therapist in 2004 in Nebraska. The majority of my career was spent in residential, long term, treatment centers for adolescents and adults including four years on an acute psychiatric unit of a hospital in Omaha. I held a variety of clinical supervisory and staff training positions during my years in residential. I started working in private practice in 2016. Licensed Professional Counselor - Mental Health (LPC-MH) South Dakota 2018 - Current. Show More Spiritual Health Student ministries works to create a safe and welcoming place where you can ask the tough questions of faith, discern your calling in life and grow in your faith alongside like-minded\n        Christians. You can be involved in student ministries regardless of your church background . It does not matter if you have gone to church all your life or if you are just curious\n                about this God-thing. We want to walk with you on your journey with Christ. You may qualify for a Scholarship. Any student who pledges to be active in student ministries at DWU may be eligible to receive a Christian Leadership award of up to $4,000. You can participate in a wide-range of activities. You will have the opportunity to participate in Thursday chapel, small group studies, worship under the stars,\n                retreats, outreach/mission projects or anything that fuels your passion to serve and worship God. We will help you find your passion and align it with your strengths. You can travel on domestic and international mission trips. Past mission trips have gone to Peru, Mexico, Kenya, Uganda and Kansas City. The trips are an\n                opportunity for students to put their faith into action and better understand the world and their role in it. Campus Worship Services We offer weekly worship experiences on campus, as well as several other seasonal and special services. All services are open to seekers and believers, to growth and\n        questions, to commitment and passion, and to service and witness. While it’s not mandatory, participating in campus ministry worship and\n        activities can help you make friends and provide you with an extensive support system. Weekly worship: 11 a.m. in the Sherman Center every Thursday. Worship Under the Stars is an evening worship centered around music, scripture and prayer. Worship Under the Stars happens in a variety of settings on\n                selected Monday nights during the semester. Fusion United Methodist Church meets every Sunday in the Sherman Center. Fusion offers a great opportunity for contemporary worship with students and those\n                from the Mitchell community. If you have any questions about campus ministry, please contact the DWU campus pastor. Grid List Taryn Ragels, M. Div. Associate Campus Pastor Lead Pastor At Fusion Church (Mitchell, SD) (2020-Present), Director of Ministries at Fusion Church (2017-2020), Community Life and College Ministry Assistant at GracePoint Wesleyan Church (Brookings, SD) The Rev. Anthony Purcell, Ph.D. Campus Pastor Senior Pastor at Lake Gibson United Methodist Church, Visiting Assistant Professor of Religion at Florida Southern College, Teaching Associate and Adjunct Professor at Emory University, Youth Minister at Lithia Springs United Methodist Church Taryn Ragels, M. Div. Associate Campus Pastor Lead Pastor At Fusion Church (Mitchell, SD) (2020-Present), Director of Ministries at Fusion Church (2017-2020), Community Life and College Ministry Assistant at GracePoint Wesleyan Church (Brookings, SD) The Rev. Anthony Purcell, Ph.D. Campus Pastor Senior Pastor at Lake Gibson United Methodist Church, Visiting Assistant Professor of Religion at Florida Southern College, Teaching Associate and Adjunct Professor at Emory University, Youth Minister at Lithia Springs United Methodist Church Show More Academic Assistance We are here to support you in your academic journey. Below are special services for you. Academic and Career Services TRIO Student Support Services Office of Disabilities Services Student Life Staff McGovern Library Purchase books IT Services The DWU Information Technology department is here to assist you with iPad, email, printing and computer questions. How to connect with IT: Email suppport@dwu.edu Call 605-995-2900 Log on to TigerNet and click TECH\n                HELP. Questions? Please email us or give us a call. 605-995-2650 admissions@dwu.edu Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
