cil Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin TRIO Student Support Services A Supportive Community TRIO Student Support Services provides you with a supportive community , from your first year through graduation . We believe that students who are first-generation, from\n        families with limited income, and those who have documented disabilities bring essential strengths with them to college. TRIO will both\n        support and challenge you to build your academic and personal strengths . The ultimate goal of the TRIO program is to increase the number of students who succeed from semester to\n        semester and who graduate from DWU. Requirements for Transfer Eligibility TRIO serves students who meet at least one of the following eligibility criteria: First generation college students. This means neither of your parents has completed a four-year degree. Students from limited income families. This is determined by taxable income. See Federal Income Guidelines . Students with disabilities. Documentation must be provided to Office of Disability\n                Services . You must be enrolled at DWU full time, meet the residency requirements for student aid, and demonstrate academic potential and\n                need. Success Services We provide proactive support services to promote your personal, academic and professional goals and provide strategies in support of those goals. Services include: Academic Tutoring Peer Mentors College Success and Study Skill Strategies Academic Advising and Course Selection Assistance Personal Counseling Financial Literacy Financial Aid and Scholarship Assistance Career and Work Preparation Post-Graduate School Planning Opportunities for Service and Leadership Opportunities for Cultural and Social Engagement Access to Campus and Community Resources Opportunities for Grant Aid Scholarship Awards (Pell-eligible) Application Process You will complete an application online during new student registration. TRIO s taff will review applications and request additional required documentation. About TRIO TRIO programs are college opportunity programs funded by the U.S. Department of Education that advocate for college access and success. Similar to student financial\n        aid programs, which help students overcome financial barriers to higher education, TRIO programs help students overcome class, social and cultural barriers to higher\n        education. In South Dakota, TRIO has 11 projects serving 2,721 participants. Dakota Wesleyan University has offered a TRIO Program since 1979 and currently serves 160\n        students. Questions? TRIO Student Support Services Dakota Wesleyan University 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 studentsuccess@dwu.edu 605-995-2901 Grid List Caleb Crist, MBA Student Success Adviser Union Lumber/Ace Hardware - Marysville, C.A. (2017-2020) | Karl's TV and Appliance - Mitchell, S.D. (Summer 2022) | Vantage Point Solutions - Mitchell, S.D. (2023-2025) Jodi Wilson, M.S.Ed. Director of TRIO Third Grade Teacher (Longfellow Elementary), Computer Teacher (John Paul II Elementary) and Contract Manager (FARR Technologies) Kelli Mueller, M.Ed. Office of Disability Services Coordinator | Student Success Adviser Mitchell School District (7th/8th grade science instructor) Luke Loudenburg, M.Ed. Student Success Adviser Tiffany Ellis, M.A. Academic Success Coordinator Fuller Center for Housing (Global Builders Program Manager & Bike Adventure Trip Leader) | Russell Media (Digital Marketing Account Manager) | Ball State University (Assistant Lecturer of ESL) | Fulbright Student Program (English Teaching Assistant (North Macedonia '12-'13)) | Ball State University (Graduate Assistant (ESL Instructor)) Caleb Crist, MBA Student Success Adviser Union Lumber/Ace Hardware - Marysville, C.A. (2017-2020) | Karl's TV and Appliance - Mitchell, S.D. (Summer 2022) | Vantage Point Solutions - Mitchell, S.D. (2023-2025) Jodi Wilson, M.S.Ed. Director of TRIO Third Grade Teacher (Longfellow Elementary), Computer Teacher (John Paul II Elementary) and Contract Manager (FARR Technologies) Kelli Mueller, M.Ed. Office of Disability Services Coordinator | Student Success Adviser Mitchell School District (7th/8th grade science instructor) Luke Loudenburg, M.Ed. Student Success Adviser Tiffany Ellis, M.A. Academic Success Coordinator Fuller Center for Housing (Global Builders Program Manager & Bike Adventure Trip Leader) | Russell Media (Digital Marketing Account Manager) | Ball State University (Assistant Lecturer of ESL) | Fulbright Student Program (English Teaching Assistant (North Macedonia '12-'13)) | Ball State University (Graduate Assistant (ESL Instructor)) Show More Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
