& Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin Hold Your Event at DWU Your Event, Our Venue Looking for the perfect venue for your next event? Dakota Wesleyan University offers a variety of flexible spaces that can be customized to fit your needs. Whether you're planning a meeting,\n        conference, banquet or simple celebration, the DWU team will help you create a memorable experience. Choose from a variety of venue setups: Theater-style setup: chairs facing the front of the room. This arrangement fits the largest number of people in the\n                space. Classroom-style setup: tables with two chairs on one side, facing the front of the room. This arrangement fits the fewest number of people\n                in the space. Dining-style setup: round tables with seven chairs per table. This arrangement is best for banquets and formal\n                events. Depending on which setup you choose, we can accommodate a variety of group sizes. In addition to our classrooms, conference rooms and outdoor space, we\n        offer: DWU/Avera Sports and Wellness Complex (track and gymnasium) Christen Family Athletic Center (gymnasium) Knox Conference Room (20-40 people) McGovern Conference Room (10-15 people) Pratt Alumni Board Room (160 people) Sherman Center (200-425 people; balcony seats 160) Catering Services Planning a meeting, banquet or special event? Say hello to D-Dub’s by CF Catering! Let our talented chefs create a customized menu, ranging from simple snacks and buffets to\n        full-service banquet meals, all crafted to fit your vision and budget. Request Catering Information Make Your Reservations We’re excited to host your group! For information regarding rates and the reservation of DWU facilities, please contact us. Grid List Jodi Landgaard, MBA Vice President of Finance & Administration Worked 20 years in corporate and private industries. Landgaard worked for 16 years at a public community college in Minnesota. She began her role as VP of Finance & Administration in August 2023. Jodi Landgaard, MBA Vice President of Finance & Administration Worked 20 years in corporate and private industries. Landgaard worked for 16 years at a public community college in Minnesota. She began her role as VP of Finance & Administration in August 2023. Show More 