ements for admission. For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Please Select... For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Life at DWU Living on campus is a great opportunity to make lifelong friends. Student Activities and Organizations We offer a variety of ways to get involved on campus. Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Please Select... Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Giving Every gift helps our students, no matter how large or small. Alumni There are many ways to stay connected to Dakota Wesleyan University. Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Please Select... Alumni & Giving President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship Athletics Performing Arts Visit Give Apply Now instagram facebook twitter linkedin ADMISSIONS Belong to a community where you matter Apply for FREE and begin an amazing new chapter in your life. You’ve already\n        started your search for a DIFFERENT kind of university education. Belong to a community where you matter. Become a force for good in\n        a swiftly changing world. Serve something larger than yourself. Ready to apply? Let’s do this! Applying at DWU is free and easy to complete. Graduating High School Seniors Transfer Students International Students A.S. in Nursing Program (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing Program (Sioux Falls Campus) RN to B.S.N. Program (Online) Graduate Students Online Students Mitchell Teachers Degree Completion (Online) Want to keep track of your application process? Download our popular DWU Admissions Checklist. Admissions Checklist International Student Application A.S. in Nursing Application Undergraduate and Transfer Application This free application is for graduating high school seniors and students transferring from another university.  It's easy, so you might as well do it now! Explore Graduate and Online Student Application If you have already earned your bachelor’s degree or you are interested in one of our specialty programs for adult students, this is the place for you. Explore ACT/SAT Test Optional At Dakota Wesleyan University, you do not have to submit your ACT or SAT test scores with your application. DWU aims to remove barriers that may impede\n        some students’ ability to pursue a Dakota Wesleyan education. With that aim, DWU does not require first-year students to submit their standardized test scores as a part of their\n        application. There are exceptions for certain students/programs where scores are required. Exceptions Student athletes At this time, because of NAIA eligibility rules, student athletes are required to submit official scores in order to be declared eligible\n                                for competition. These scores are submitted to both DWU and the NAIA. International students International students are still required to submit English Language Test Scores (TOEFL, IELTS, PTE) or College Preparation Test Scores\n                                (ACT, SAT) for admission consideration. Homeschooled students without a transcript Early Admission (Direct-Entry) Nursing Applicants Students wishing to be considered for direct-entry admission into our nursing program should submit test scores. Students who choose not to\n                                submit test scores during the application process may still declare a nursing major but will apply for entry into the program during their second year at\n                                DWU. Other outside scholarships Scholarships offered by entities other than DWU may require a standardized test score, including but not limited to Dakota Corps, South\n                                Dakota Opportunity Scholarship and others. Not R eady to A pply Y et? That’s totally fine. The best way to determine whether DWU is the place for you is to\n        visit. When you visit, one of our student ambassadors will guide your tour of\n        campus . We have new, student-centered academic and recreational buildings, our outdoor space is beautiful and the people you meet will welcome you warmly to our community. Shake hands with our professors and get to know our diverse student body as you absorb what it means to be a Tiger. Schedule your visit today. Schedule a Visit Important Admission Information We also want you to know that no applicant will be denied admission because of race, color, religion, national origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender or gender\n        identity, genetic information, age or other impermissible factors. The university reserves the right to deny admission or continued enrollment to any student who imposes an unreasonable risk\n        of harm to the health, safety, welfare or property of the university, members of the university community or him/herself. Please also note that some of our programs have special requirements for admission, so if you are denied admission into athletic training , education or nursing , you may be eligible for admission into other\n        programs. Higher Learning Commission DWU is institutionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Questions? If you can’t find the answer to your question, give us a call at 605-995-2600 or contact us any time online. We look forward to welcoming you! Meet Our Admissions Staff Grid List Tatum Dean Campus Visit Coordinator Admissions Health Information and Quality Assurance Specialist at Seneca Family of Agencies (2022-2024) | Youth Counselor at Seneca Family of Agencies (2021-2022) | English Teacher at Chungdahm Learning Inc. in South Korea (2019-2020) LaNae Fuerst Admissions Counselor Admissions I taught Family and Consumer Sciences (FACS) for three years in Gettysburg, S.D. I then took a job closer to home and taught FACS for three years at Corsica-Stickney, before becoming an admissions counselor at Dakota Wesleyan University. Rachel Giblin Associate Director of Admissions Admissions Janet Greenway Graduate & Online Enrollment Coordinator Admissions 1 yr. (1989): Dakota Wesleyan University: Resident Director of Dayton Hall, 4 yrs. (1990-1994): Dakota Wesleyan University: Admissions Counselor, 29 yrs. (1994-2023): Mitchell Technical College: Admissions Counselor, Career Services, Academic Advising, and Registrar Corbin Kramer Performing Arts Talent Coordinator Admissions, Music, Theatre Laurie Martin Enrollment Services Specialist Admissions Queen of Peace Hospital (Radiologic Technologist, 15 years), City of Mitchell (Communications Specialist, 10+ years), Martin Group (Administrative Assistant, 9 years) Megan Sarne Admissions Counselor Admissions Taught for three years at Red Rock Central in Lamberton, Minnesota, and two years at Longfellow Elementary in Mitchell, South Dakota. Fredel Thomas, MBA Vice President of Admissions, Marketing and Technology Admissions, Marketing and Communications, Information Technology Fredel started her career at DWU as director of the Kelly Center for Entrepreneurship, where she taught entrepreneurial leadership courses and served as a resource for regional businesses in South Dakota. She was named dean of admissions in 2015 and was promoted to vice president of admissions and marketing in 2018. As an extension to her work at DWU, Fredel served as chair of the Council on College Admissions in South Dakota, is a board member of the Dakota  Association for College Admission Counseling, serves on the South Dakota Freedom Scholarship Advisory Council, is an affiliate for Credo, a higher education consulting firm, and a frequent speaker for the National Small College Enrollment Conference. Prior to DWU, Fredel worked 12 years in the telecommunications and technology industry as a programmer, quality assurance officer, project manager and director of product management. She has served as a board member for the Weekend Snack Pack, the Abbott House, the Mitchell Area Chamber of Commerce, the Safe Place of Eastern South Dakota, and Avera Queen of Peace. She is active in her church where she leads youth group. Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Back Department: Location: Phone: Campus Mail Box: Year Started at DWU: Education History: Professional History: Strengths: Area of Expertise: Hobbies: Family: What I Love Most About DWU: Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy MozBar\n\nTop\nDomains\nLinks\nKeywords\nSpam\nDomains\nLinks\nKeywords\nBA\nGet access to all metrics in MozBar\nTry Moz Pro Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
