nds. Alumni Welcome Center L ocated on the east side of campus. H ouses the\n        institutional advancement and alumni offices. Dakota Discovery Museum and DWU Black Box Theatre located within the building. Christen Family Athletic Center Built in 1985, this space is h ome to the DWU athletic department, strength and conditioning weight room, athletic training space, and the Fosness Arena, named legendary DWU basketball coach Gordie Fosness. Dakota Hall Our newest residence hall for upperclassm e n. Private bathrooms , c ommunity space s, study room s, kitchenette s and community laundry room . Dayton Hall Freshman residence hall with traditional 2-person\n        rooms. L ounge on each floor , l aundry and kitchen facilities , main lobby gathering\n        space . DWU Suites I ndependent living for juniors and seniors. P rivate bath, living area, kitchenette with refrigerator and central heating /AC in each\n        unit . A ttached to Allen Hall\n        by a common lobby . Choice\n        of studio, one- or two- bedroom unit s. DWU/Avera Sports and Wellness L ocated on the south side of campus, across Norway Avenue from the Christen Family Athletic Center. 87,000-plus-square-foot, one-story facility. I ncludes fitness center, DWU athletic training facilities, 200-meter track, large field house with\n        multiple sports courts, wrestling room, locker rooms, classrooms. DWU Theatre 5 ,000-square-foot space located on the south\n        side of campus within the Alumni Welcome Center. H ouses a black-box theatre, scene\n        shop, office space, dressing rooms, bathrooms and a green room . Education Department H oused in the east end of the L.B. Williams public elementary school and attached to the Christen\n        Family Athletic Center. Faculty offices and classrooms with large tv screens. Glenda K. Corrigan Health Sciences Center F our-story, 48,000-square-foot building hous ing chemistry, biology and physics\n        labs . T wo undergraduate research labs equipped with the latest\n        equipment . F our nursing simulation labs . C lassrooms for nursing, athletic training, the science s, mathematics and faculty\n        offices. Jackson Plaza A rich, inviting landscap e including a centralized courtyard, a water feature and illuminated trees . A favorite gathering place for students, faculty and staff. Koka Hall A co - ed residence hall with laundry facilities and\n        a fully equipped kitchen. McGovern Library H ome to the McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service, the campus store , Tiger Café, the archives of the Dakotas Conference of the United Methodist Church, the DWU Archives, the McGovern Legacy Museum and all DWU library\n        services. P rivate study spaces, faculty offices, TR I O Student Support Services, classrooms and the digital media and design\n        department. Pepsi-Cola Soccer Complex L ocated north of Mitchell near the Mitchell Municipal Airport on Tower Road. F eatures 10 soccer fields, including Championship Field – a fully lighted, 80 x 120-yard field with a seating capacity of 620\n        fans , locker rooms, athletic training rooms an officials' room and a two-story\n        press box. Rollins Campus Center S tudent-centric building including a dmissions\n        office, campus pastor, dean of students , Wagner Chapel , c ampus nurse, campus counselor, financial aid, registrar, business office, mail room, residence life\n        and student activities offices. D-Dub's, DWU's dining hall, and meeting\n        rooms are located on the second floor. School of Business, Innovation and Leadership DWU’s newest building featuring 30,000 sq uare -f ee t devoted to business programs , housing the Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship, a large, multipurpose boardroom and\n        community meeting space, entrepreneurship ideation labs and a media marketing\n        commons . Sherman Center A ttached the Rollins Campus Center. The campus’ main event center for concerts, alumni gatherings and weekly c hapel service s . Smith Hall Home to the Ron and Sheilah Gates Department of Music, office of the president, vice president and provost, the IT department and helpdesk, coaches’ offices, esports lab,\n        marketing department, and the communications, religion, psychology departments. Wagner Chapel L ocated between the Sherman Center and Rollins Campus Center. P rovides an intimate setting for students to mediate or pray. Questions? Please email us or give us a call. Email: admissions@dwu.edu Phone: 605-995-2650 Quick Links Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Check Links Check SEO × SEO Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Performance × Performance Report Placeholder issue 1: This is a test issue. Placeholder issue 2: Another test issue. Check Accessibility Quick Links Menu Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy Accessibility High Contrast Dark White text on black backgrounds (WCAG-style) High Contrast Light Black text on white backgrounds (WCAG-style) Grayscale Remove colors from page Highlight Links Make links stand out clearly Dyslexia Friendly Use easier-to-read font Text Spacing Increase line & letter spacing Reading Guide Highlight current line while reading Large Cursor Increase cursor size Hide Images Hide all images on the page Core Controls Reset 100% Text Size 100% Line Height 1.5 Letter Spacing 0px Reset All"
